# basePath Chapter2

:: FirstContractOpenCh2
@trigger    OnContractSelectOpen
@cutscene
@once

//NOTE - should dialogue/tutorializing be prompted in mini-games? 

{@Dorian}   Alright my friend, or "employee", looks you'll need a conductor and semi-conductor. 
{@Dorian}   With semi-conductors you will be working on doping. 
{@Dorian}   Essentially, adding impurities to the semi-conductor make it, well, conductive. 
{@Player}   Okay, great, so, when I go about doing it--
{@Dorian}   Oh shoot, sorry Locke, I'm getting a halo, I have to go. 
{@Dorian}   P.A.L. should be able to help you out though!
{@Player}   Yea, no worries. 
{@Dorian}   Chat soon. 

{@PAL}      Sounded like you had a question Captain, can I be of assitance? 
{@Player}   Uh... I forgot it...       
{@PAL}      Alrighty then, Captian! 

$call   LockWikiPage("Basic Conductor") // Basic Conductor is replaced with the full version after first chapter 
$call   LockWikiPage("Basic Insulator") // Basic Insulator is replaced with the full version after first chapter 
$call   UnlockWikiPage("Conductor")
$call   UnlockWikiPage("Insulator")

::BeforeSupplyChainCh2
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene
@once

//region Suppliers 
//NOTE - under context of being in mini-game 
{@Player}   Hey P.A.L., why are there two sources of Phosphorus? 
{@PAL}      Looks like both the Forsch and Kalvis sectors are offering that material. 
{@Player}   What's the difference? 
{@PAL}      Depending on which one they may have different costs and time sinks.
{@PAL}      I highly recommend going with the Forsch sector. 
{@Player}   Are you seriously recommending that? 
{@Player}   Or are you saying that because that's a Frontier sector? 
{@PAL}      A Froniter Robotics deal is always a good deal! 
{@Player}   Let me call each, then I'll decide. 

//#region - Kalvis & Forsch Sector 

{@Player}   Hi Taryn.
{@Taryn}    Locke, hiya!
{@Player}   Listen I saw... your face, you got uh... dirt all over it. 
{@Taryn}    Oh! I was in my garden earlier, got a bit lost in the weeds!  
{@Taryn}    Anywhosies. Let me guess, you're calling about the new Phosphorus station? 
{@PAL}      Seems like a conference call can speed up your decision. Let me patch you to the Forsch Sector! 
{@Player}   Wait no, P.A.L.
{@PAL}      Call connected! 
{@Ovill}    Hello Locke! I got another deal for you. Our new Phosphorus station will blow your noodle!
{@Taryn}    Ovill.
{@Ovill}    Taryn.
{@Taryn}    So, trying to steal my client? 
{@Ovill}    Rich, coming from a deserter. 
{@Player}   ...Do you guys know each other? 
{@Taryn}    I... worked at Frontier Robotics once upon a time.
{@Taryn}    But I left. 
{@Ovill}    Taryn here decided that working with traitors was a better option. 
{@Taryn}    At least I didn't sell my soul to a mega-corp.
{@Ovill}    And to think you were a rising star. 
{@Taryn}    Whatever. Frontier has a gazillion rising stars. I wasn't special.
{@Taryn}    Neither are you, or anyone trying to climb Frontier's ladder. 
{@Ovill}    I'll have you know I have the highest marks out of my entire department. 
{@Player}   Hey guys... the Phosphorus...
{@Ovill}    Hm? Oh yes! We have a Phosphorus station available to you in rapid speed! 
{@Ovill}    Just to remind you that there will be a sourcing fee, a labor fee, a buying fee-
{@Taryn}    Oh, don't forget the breathing fee.
{@Ovill}    -_-
{@Taryn}    Or you can source from us! It'll take a bit longer but you'll have genunine product at a fair price. 
{@Player}   I'll think about it. Thanks guys. 


